// PILOT: first player-cast use of `SpriteSummon` (previously NPC/weapon-only
// -- `custom/dwarves/forgemaster/`, `custom/gigas_frost/`,
// `custom/harvester/`, etc.). Documenting its real shape here since nothing
// established one for a player spell before this file.
//
// `SpriteSummon`'s struct (common/src/comp/ability.rs) is: buildup/cast/
// recover durations, a `SpriteKind` to place, `del_timeout` (despawn
// window), `summon_distance` (radius grown over `cast_duration`), `anchor`,
// `sparseness`, `angle`, `move_efficiency`, `ori_modifier`, `meta`. There is
// no `energy_cost` field on this variant at all (checked the struct
// directly, not assumed) -- every existing NPC use is free to cast, and so
// is this spell; that is a real engine gap for a player-facing ability, not
// a balance choice made here. There is also no damage, buff, or trigger-on-
// disturb field of any kind: `create_sprites`
// (common/src/states/sprite_summon.rs) only ever emits `CreateSpriteEvent`,
// nothing else. The two existing precedents that come closest to "a hidden
// dormant ward" (`custom/cursekeeper/trap.ron`, `custom/terracotta_statue/
// trap.ron`, both `sprite: Empty`) are purely a buildup-stage charge-
// telegraph visual (`Outcome::TerracottaStatueCharge`) for a *separate*
// damaging ability fired elsewhere in that NPC's kit -- there is no second
// "the glyph goes off" ability slot to pair with here, and Lane A rules out
// writing one (no new `CharacterAbility` variant/field, no new Rust).
//
// D&D's actual payoff -- "erupts with an elemental burst, or releases a
// bound spell, when disturbed" -- is therefore **not deliverable** by this
// variant as it exists today: no trigger condition, no damage, no buff. What
// *is* real and observable: `EnsnaringVines` sprites (the same low-traction
// obstruction terrain/block.rs already grants -- 0.1 traction, same table
// entangle.ron's `DifficultTerrain` zone effect layers on top of, not
// invented here) placed in a growing ring around the touched spot, matching
// the sheet's own `Sphere r6` aoe and lingering for a while
// (`del_timeout`). This ships as a real, if secondary and much weaker,
// mechanical footprint -- a rune-marked patch of warded ground that's
// physically awkward to walk through -- rather than either inventing an
// undeliverable trigger/burst or shipping a pure no-op. The burst/trigger
// payload is dropped entirely and is the actual content debt this pilot
// leaves open: a real "disturb this glyph -> stored effect fires" mechanic
// needs a new `CharacterAbility` shape (Lane B), not a Lane A content pass.
SpriteSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    sprite: EnsnaringVines,
    del_timeout: Some((600.0, 60.0)),
    summon_distance: (0.0, 6.0),
    sparseness: 0.5,
    angle: 360.0,
    anchor: Summoner,
    move_efficiency: 1.0,
    ori_modifier: 1.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
